
🚀 Release v1.0.0 — Backend Architecture & API Specifications
We are excited to publish the complete Backend Architecture and API Specifications for the Cleaning Sewa / Career Application module.

This release provides full technical specifications, database schemas, and Node.js REST API standards designed to support the React Native mobile application.

📋 What's Included
1. Database Schema (CareerApplication)
Complete Mongoose / PostgreSQL data specifications.

Strict validation rules for candidate details, Nepal phone formats (10 digits), position limits, and experience metrics.

Structured array storage for document URLs (ID proofs, training certificates).

2. API Endpoints
POST /api/v1/careers/apply — Public application submission controller.

POST /api/v1/files/upload — Multipart file upload handler with strict .jpg, .jpeg, and .png extension filters (5MB per file limit).

GET /api/v1/careers — Administrative portal listing endpoint.

3. Middleware & Security Features
Input validation and payload sanitization via express-validator.

Disk storage routing via multer.

Error-handling pipeline and status code normalization.

🛠️ Tech Stack Guidelines
Runtime: Node.js (Express.js / NestJS)

Database: MongoDB (Mongoose) or PostgreSQL (Prisma)

File Storage: Local Static Server / AWS S3 / Cloudinary

Authentication: JWT (JSON Web Tokens)

